Why: design 10 P4, interpretation rule 4: a code that is not in codes.py is kept in unknown_messages and shown as
TLC printed it; at severity 1 it is an error (kind other), at severity 3 a warning, at severity 0 an UnknownMessage.
No capture has a code outside the table.

How: a copy of tlc/v1.7.4/violation.out with the code of three messages changed, in their start and end markers:
2110 (severity 1, "Invariant Small is violated.") to 9901, 2401 (severity 3, the garbage collector warning) to 9902,
and 2190 (severity 0, "Finished computing initial states") to 9903. 9901 to 9903 are in no TLC table that design 10
P4 and P5 list and not in src/tlaup/tlc/codes.py (checked 2026-11-25); the captures use 9999 only as text a spec
prints. Nothing else changed.
